From: hiper25 <whydonit@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec: retain the full Request source append extent

Native frame-based HEVC packs each slice into the same OUTPUT object.
qent_src_data_copy() reserves and writes offset + len bytes, but reported
only len as the object's used size. Multi-slice frames therefore reached
QBUF with only the final slice length despite containing every original
NAL, and the kernel correctly rejected the earlier slice span.

Report the complete written extent. Offset-zero callers still replace the
used size, including when a reused buffer receives a shorter new frame.
No coded bytes, controls, allocations or completion checks are changed.

--- a/libavcodec/v4l2_req_media.c
+++ b/libavcodec/v4l2_req_media.c
@@ -939,7 +939,7 @@
     if (!dst)
         return -1;
     memcpy((char*)dst + offset, src, len);
-    dmabuf_len_set(be->dh[0], len);
+    dmabuf_len_set(be->dh[0], offset + len);
     dmabuf_write_end(be->dh[0]);
     return 0;
 }
